      ['t06', 'The road', 'resolve', 0.86, `${C.ashtavakra} walks along a long road with his wooden staff toward a distant royal city, determined.`,
        'So the boy with the bent body set out… for King Janaka’s court.'],
      ['t07', 'The gate', 'pained', 0.82, `At a palace gate, tall guards laugh and block the way of ${C.ashtavakra}, pointing at him.`,
        'At the gate, the guards laughed. Children are not allowed in the hall of scholars.'],
      ['t08', 'The elder', 'firm', 0.84, `${C.ashtavakra} stands calm and tall in spirit before the palace guards, speaking firmly, one hand raised, and the guards fall silent.`,
        'Ashtavakra said: a person is not old because of grey hair. The one who knows… is the elder.'],
      ['t09', 'Laughter', 'pained', 0.82, `In a grand royal hall full of scholars in white and saffron, everyone bursts out laughing and pointing at ${C.ashtavakra} as he walks in with his staff.`,
        'When he walked into the hall, every scholar burst out laughing… at his crooked body.'],
      ['t10', 'Skin', 'firm', 0.84, `In the royal hall, ${C.ashtavakra} laughs back calmly at the scholars, who stop and stare, embarrassed.`,
        'And then Ashtavakra laughed too. The story goes he said: I thought I had come to a gathering of the wise. But you only see skin and bones.'],
      ['t11', 'Bowed', 'wonder', 0.84, `${C.janaka} comes down from his throne and bows respectfully to ${C.ashtavakra}, as the hall falls silent.`,
        'The hall fell silent. King Janaka came down from his throne… and bowed to the boy.'],
      ['t12', 'Debate', 'grand', 0.86, `In the royal hall, ${C.ashtavakra} debates ${C.bandi}, the boy speaking with confidence while the proud scholar looks defeated, the court watching.`,
        'Then he faced Bandi, the great scholar, in debate… and won.'],
      ['t13', 'Father', 'joyful', 0.86, `At the edge of a river, a brahmin with a black beard rises from the water and embraces ${C.ashtavakra}, both weeping with joy.`,
        'And his father came back from the waters… alive.'],
      ['t14', 'Samanga', 'sacred', 0.82, `${C.ashtavakra} steps out of a sacred river at sunrise, and his body is now straight and whole, his face peaceful, his father watching from the bank.`,
        'The story goes that his father told him to bathe in the river Samanga. And when he came out… his body was straight.'],
      ['t15', 'Witness', 'sacred', 0.82, `Ashtavakra, now a calm young sage in white robes, sits teaching ${C.janaka}, who sits humbly as his student in a garden at dusk.`,
        'Later, King Janaka became his student. Their talks became the Ashtavakra Gita: you are not the body… you are the one who watches.'],
      ['diya', 'The knower', 'peace', 0.8, null,
        'Krishna says in the Gita… This body is called the field. And the one who knows it… is called the knower of the field.']
